# Fleet static = live WordPress

WordPress on hosting IP `174.136.29.214` is the source of truth. Static must match the **current** WP snapshot, never an old KV copy.

## Refresh / cutover (use this, not KV-to-KV migrate)

Live WP → scrape via hosting IP → `HTML_FLEET` + `fleet-static-assets` → `fleet-static-worker`.

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\Invoke-WpOriginToFleet.ps1 -SitesCsv .\reports\{csv} -HostingIp 174.136.29.214
```

Do **not** use `Invoke-MigrateSitesToFleet.ps1` to refresh content (that copies stale per-site KV).
Do **not** use `static-conversion\scripts\Invoke-DeepAssetSync.ps1` on fleet sites (it writes `{domain}-worker` keys, not `{host}:html:` / `{host}:asset:`).

## Edit workflow

1. Rollback to WordPress (Worker route off; keep KV/R2)
2. Edit and verify on live WP
3. Scrape latest WP into `HTML_FLEET` + `fleet-static-assets`
4. Switch routes back to `fleet-static-worker`
5. Verify public site: `200`, `x-source: kv`, `x-fleet-host`, HTML/CSS/JS/images/forms match origin WP

## Guardrails

- Stay-WordPress excludes: never convert or fleet-migrate
- Do not delete old per-site Workers until the fleet snapshot is verified and stable
- After refresh, confirm no stale KV content is still being served
- After every scrape/promote, SVGs must be `image/svg+xml` (never `application/xml`). Adam API and origin-fill have stored rating badges as XML, which shows as broken `<img>` placeholders. The fleet Worker forces SVG content-type; scrape scripts also re-PUT homepage SVGs.
